WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.477
Join now asks the ride hub for your seat, and a full or started session sends you to

00:00:07.477 --> 00:00:08.535
the next one.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:14.761
Press Join, and the ride connects to the hub and takes a seat in that session, with

00:00:14.761 --> 00:00:16.505
a jersey colour of its own.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.195
With ten riders seated, the hub says the session is full, and Class Start offers the

00:00:28.195 --> 00:00:30.032
one fifteen minutes later.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.587
Arrive after the start, and the hub turns you away. Class Start shows the next

00:00:40.587 --> 00:00:41.801
session instead.

00:00:46.457 --> 00:00:51.160
If the link drops, the ride asks again as soon as it is back, and keeps the same

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:51.754
seat.

00:00:59.361 --> 00:01:03.539
The group ride looks the same on every screen, with your seat held underneath.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.954
What the tests prove: a seat until the start, ten at most, the next session offered,

00:01:16.954 --> 00:01:18.593
and the same seat again.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:27.193
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:01:27.538 --> 00:01:32.050
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.721
every hill and interval.

00:01:34.066 --> 00:01:39.244
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:01:39.244 --> 00:01:44.692
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:01:44.692 --> 00:01:47.682
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:01:48.027 --> 00:01:50.520
A custom workout lives under Profile.
